Problem - Contain Duplicates (Leetcode = 217)

Aim - Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

Algorithm -
1. Start
2. Read the input array nums.
3. Sort the array in ascending order.
4. Traverse the array from index 1 to len(nums) - 1.
5. Compare the current element nums[i] with the previous element nums[i - 1].
6. If both elements are equal:
7. Return True (duplicate found).
8. If the loop finishes without finding any duplicate:
9. Return False (all elements are distinct).
10. End

Code - 
class Solution(object):
    def containsDuplicate(self, nums):
        """
        :type nums: List[int]
        :rtype: bool
        """
        nums.sort()

        for i in range(1, len(nums)):
            if nums[i] == nums[i - 1]:
                return True

        return False

